  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ameneen Initiation Phase: Establishing a Nationally Led Refugee&#x2013;Migrant&#x2013;Host Community Response Architecture in Egypt</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Ameneen Initiation Phase establishes the core foundations for Egypt&#x2019;s first nationally coordinated mechanism for refugees, migrants, and host communities, aligning with the Asylum Law No. 164/2024, Vision 2030, and the UNSDCF. Over four months, UNDP, working with UNHCR, IOM, and the UNRCO, will support MoSS and MoFA in designing Ameneen&#x2019;s governance model, financing framework, evidence-based, and multi-year response plan outline, ensuring Egypt is fully equipped to operationalize a nationall</narrative>
  </description>
